{"task_id": "HumanEval/17", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Dict\n\n# 3.1. Data Structures / 3.2. Algorithm Step 1: Define the constant NOTE_TO_BEATS map\nNOTE_TO_BEATS: Dict[str, int] = {'o': 4, 'o|': 2, '.|': 1}\n\ndef parse_music(music_string: str) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Parses a string of musical notes in a special ASCII format and returns a\n    list of integers corresponding to the beat duration of each note.\n\n    Args:\n        music_string: A string containing musical note tokens ('o', 'o|', '.|')\n                      separated by one or more spaces.\n\n    Returns:\n        An ordered list of integers, where each integer is the beat duration\n        of the corresponding note in the input string.\n\n    Raises:\n        TypeError: When the input provided is not a string.\n        ValueError: When the input string contains a token that is not a\n                    valid, recognized note representation.\n    \"\"\"\n    # 3.2. Algorithm Step 3: Validate input type\n    if not isinstance(music_string, str):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a string.\")\n\n    # 3.2. Algorithm Step 4: Pre-process the input string\n    processed_string = music_string.strip()\n\n    # 3.2. Algorithm Step 5: Handle empty string case\n    if not processed_string:\n        return []\n\n    # 3.2. Algorithm Step 6: Split the string into tokens\n    tokens = processed_string.split()\n\n    # 3.2. Algorithm Step 7: Initialize result list\n    result_beats: List[int] = []\n\n    # 3.2. Algorithm Steps 8-11: Iterate, translate, and handle errors\n    for token in tokens:\n        try:\n            beat_value = NOTE_TO_BEATS[token]\n            result_beats.append(beat_value)\n        except KeyError:\n            raise ValueError(f'Invalid note token found: \"{token}\"')\n\n    # 3.2. Algorithm Step 12: Return the result\n    return result_beats\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/18", "solution": "```python\ndef how_many_times(string: str, substring: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the total number of overlapping occurrences of a substring within a string.\n\n    Args:\n        string: The main string in which to search.\n        substring: The substring to count occurrences of.\n\n    Returns:\n        The total number of overlapping occurrences.\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If the provided substring is an empty string.\n    \"\"\"\n    # 1. Input Validation\n    if not substring:\n        raise ValueError(\"Substring cannot be empty\")\n\n    string_len = len(string)\n    substring_len = len(substring)\n\n    # 2. Early Exit Check\n    if substring_len > string_len:\n        return 0\n\n    # 3. Initialization\n    count = 0\n\n    # 4. Iteration and Matching\n    for i in range(string_len - substring_len + 1):\n        if string.startswith(substring, i):\n            count += 1\n\n    # 5. Return Value\n    return count\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/19", "solution": "```python\nimport collections.abc\n\n# 4.1 Word-to-Integer Map\nWORD_TO_INT_MAP: dict[str, int] = {\n    'zero': 0, 'one': 1, 'two': 2, 'three': 3, 'four': 4,\n    'five': 5, 'six': 6, 'seven': 7, 'eight': 8, 'nine': 9\n}\n\n# 4.2 Integer-to-Word Map\nINT_TO_WORD_MAP: list[str] = [\n    'zero', 'one', 'two', 'three', 'four',\n    'five', 'six', 'seven', 'eight', 'nine'\n]\n\ndef sort_numbers(numbers: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Accepts a space-delimited string of English number words ('zero' to 'nine')\n    and returns a new string with the words sorted by numerical value.\n\n    Args:\n        numbers: A string containing space-delimited English words for numbers\n                 'zero' through 'nine'.\n\n    Returns:\n        A string with the input number words sorted in ascending numerical\n        order, delimited by single spaces.\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If the input string contains words not in the valid set.\n    \"\"\"\n    # 3.1.3 Step 1: Input Handling\n    if not numbers.strip():\n        return \"\"\n\n    # 3.1.3 Step 2: Parsing\n    word_tokens = numbers.split()\n\n    # 3.1.3 Step 3: Word-to-Integer Conversion\n    integer_list: list[int] = []\n    try:\n        for token in word_tokens:\n            integer_list.append(WORD_TO_INT_MAP[token])\n    except KeyError as e:\n        # Per specification, raise ValueError for invalid words\n        raise ValueError(f\"Invalid number word found: {e}\") from e\n\n    # 3.1.3 Step 4: Numerical Sorting\n    integer_list.sort()\n\n    # 3.1.3 Step 5: Integer-to-Word Conversion\n    sorted_words: list[str] = [INT_TO_WORD_MAP[num] for num in integer_list]\n\n    # 3.1.3 Step 6: Output Formatting\n    result = \" \".join(sorted_words)\n\n    # 3.1.3 Step 7: Return\n    return result\n```"}
