{"task_id": "HumanEval/21", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\ndef rescale_to_unit(numbers: List[float]) -> List[float]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Performs min-max normalization on a list of numbers, scaling them to a\n    unit interval of [0, 1].\n\n    This function follows a simple data-flow architecture. It validates the\n    input, handles edge cases like zero range, and applies a linear\n    transformation to scale each number.\n\n    Args:\n        numbers: An input list of floating-point numbers. It must contain\n                 at least two elements.\n\n    Returns:\n        A new list of the same length, with values scaled to the range [0, 1].\n        The original list is not modified.\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If the input `numbers` list contains fewer than two elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    # 1. Input Validation: Check the length of the input list.\n    if len(numbers) < 2:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input list must contain at least two elements.\")\n\n    # 2. Determine Minima and Maxima.\n    min_val = min(numbers)\n    max_val = max(numbers)\n\n    # 3. Calculate Range and Handle Zero-Range Edge Case.\n    range_val = max_val - min_val\n\n    # If all elements are identical, the range is 0.\n    # To prevent ZeroDivisionError, return a list of 0.0s.\n    if range_val == 0:\n        return [0.0] * len(numbers)\n\n    # 4. Perform Scaling Transformation using a list comprehension.\n    # The formula is: scaled_num = (num - min_val) / range_val\n    scaled_numbers = [(num - min_val) / range_val for num in numbers]\n\n    # 5. Return Result.\n    return scaled_numbers\n```"}
