{"task_id": "HumanEval/37", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Any\n\ndef sort_even(l: List[Any]) -> List[Any]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts elements at the even indices of a list while preserving the elements\n    and their positions at the odd indices.\n\n    Args:\n        l (list): The input list of sortable elements.\n\n    Returns:\n        list: A new list with elements at even indices sorted, and elements\n        at odd indices in their original positions.\n    \"\"\"\n    # 3.1. Even-Value Extractor:\n    # Extract elements located at even indices (0, 2, 4, ...).\n    even_values = l[0::2]\n\n    # 3.2. Sorting Engine:\n    # Sort the temporary list of even-indexed elements.\n    even_values.sort()\n\n    # 3.3. List Reconstructor:\n    # Create a copy of the original input list.\n    result_list = l[:]\n    \n    # Place the sorted elements back into the copied list at their\n    # corresponding even-indexed positions.\n    result_list[0::2] = even_values\n\n    return result_list\n```"}
