{"task_id": "HumanEval/55", "solution": "```python\ndef fib(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates and returns the n-th number in the Fibonacci sequence.\n\n    The sequence is defined such that fib(0) = 0, fib(1) = 1, fib(2) = 1, etc.\n    This implementation uses an efficient iterative approach with O(n) time\n    and O(1) space complexity.\n\n    Args:\n        n: The non-negative index of the Fibonacci number to compute.\n\n    Returns:\n        The n-th Fibonacci number.\n\n    Raises:\n        TypeError: Raised if the input `n` is not of type `int`.\n        ValueError: Raised if the input `n` is a negative integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    # 1. Input Validation\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be an integer.\")\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input must be a non-negative integer.\")\n\n    # 2. Base Case Handling\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    # 3. Iterative Calculation\n    a, b = 0, 1\n    for _ in range(n - 1):\n        a, b = b, a + b\n\n    # 4. Return Value\n    return b\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/56", "solution": "```python\ndef correct_bracketing(brackets: str):\n    \"\"\" brackets is a string of \"<\" and \">\".\n    return True if every opening bracket has a corresponding closing bracket.\n\n    >>> correct_bracketing(\"<\")\n    False\n    >>> correct_bracketing(\"<>\")\n    True\n    >>> correct_bracketing(\"<<><>>\")\n    True\n    >>> correct_bracketing(\"><<>\")\n    False\n    \"\"\"\n    balance = 0\n    for bracket in brackets:\n        if bracket == '<':\n            balance += 1\n        else:\n            balance -= 1\n        if balance < 0:\n            return False\n    return balance == 0\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/57", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Union\n\ndef monotonic(l: List[Union[int, float]]) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if a given list of numbers is monotonic.\n\n    A list is monotonic if its elements, from left to right, are either\n    entirely non-increasing or entirely non-decreasing.\n\n    Args:\n        l: A list of numbers (integers or floats).\n\n    Returns:\n        True if the list is monotonic, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    # 3.2.2. Edge Case Handling:\n    # Check if the length of the list l is less than or equal to 1.\n    if len(l) <= 1:\n        return True\n\n    # 3.2.3. Initialization:\n    # Initialize two boolean flags.\n    is_non_decreasing = True\n    is_non_increasing = True\n\n    # 3.2.4. Single-Pass Iteration:\n    # Loop through the list up to the second-to-last element.\n    for i in range(len(l) - 1):\n        # 3.2.5. Comparison Logic:\n        # If an element is greater than the next, it can't be non-decreasing.\n        if l[i] > l[i+1]:\n            is_non_decreasing = False\n        # If an element is less than the next, it can't be non-increasing.\n        if l[i] < l[i+1]:\n            is_non_increasing = False\n\n    # 3.2.6. Final Evaluation:\n    # The list is monotonic if it's non-increasing OR non-decreasing.\n    return is_non_decreasing or is_non_increasing\n```"}
